# ─── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEVER commit .env. It holds JWT_SECRET, the Flutterwave secret key and the
# webhook signing secrets. Anything pushed to GitHub is public forever, even if
# you delete it in a later commit — the old commit keeps the value. If a secret
# does get pushed, rotating it is the only real fix.
#
# Commit .env.example instead: same keys, placeholder values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ─── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
.Python
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# ─── Tests / tooling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/

